      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "This belongs on RADAR because the center of gravity is Cables's own writing, not a standards set wrapped around a famous pianist. Sarah Elizabeth Charles has already turned several of his instrumental pieces into songs by writing lyrics for them, while Craig Handy, Essiet Okon Essiet, and Jerome Jennings give the music enough history and flexibility to keep the songbook alive rather than fixed. It is a useful chance to hear a major living pianist-composer presented through his own vocabulary in the kind of room where touch, pacing, and ensemble response are the point.",
          "trip_verdict": "Keep it on the board if New York is already in play and take a set if it fits the schedule. The five-night run offers enough flexibility that I would not build a dedicated DMV-to-New York trip around it or displace a rarer premiere, farewell, reunion, or one-off.",
